   "id": "cs00",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Case study — decision-tree distributional query\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the DT approach end-to-end on a dataset of your choice, the same pipeline the\n",
    "UI (`quaero_ui.py`) uses — both import it from `quaero_core.py`.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Dataset** — point at a CSV; `datasets/metadata.py` supplies its delimiter,\n",
    "   target(s), id columns and categoricals when it knows the file.\n",
    "2. **Preprocessing** — drop ids and the *other* declared targets, integer-encode\n",
    "   categoricals, drop NaN/inf rows, bin the target with Scott's rule.\n",
    "3. **Index** — purity-grown decision tree over the descriptors.\n",
    "4. **Query** — specify the target distribution as a mixture, then query by\n",
    "   cardinality (disjoint subsets under a TVD threshold) or by number of boxes.\n",
    "5. **Plots** — the specified pdf, and each found subset against the full data,\n",
    "   as in the UI, plus TVD / JSD / KLD / Hellinger / BC.\n",
    "\n",
    "Edit the cells marked **✏️**, then run top to bottom."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 36,
   "id": "cs01",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "metadata known for 2 datasets\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
