    "## 4. Specify the distributional query ✏️\n",
    "\n",
    "`COMPONENTS` is a mixture: a list of `(family, params, weight)`. Weights are\n",
    "normalised. Families and their parameters:\n",
    "\n",
    "| family | params |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `gaussian` | `loc`, `scale` |\n",
    "| `exponential` | `loc`, `scale` |\n",
    "| `uniform` | `loc`, `scale` (support `[loc, loc+scale]`) |\n",
    "| `beta` | `a`, `b`, and `loc`, `scale` to stretch it off `[0, 1]` onto the target's range |\n",
    "| `weibull` | `shape`, `scale`, `loc` |\n",
    "| `lognormal` | `mu`, `sigma`, `loc` (ln(X − loc) ~ N(mu, sigma²)) |\n",
    "| `pareto` | `alpha`, `scale`, `loc` (support `x ≥ loc + scale`) |\n",
    "\n",
    "Shapes, scales and `sigma` must be > 0; an invalid value raises an error.\n",
    "\n",
    "The defaults below put one Gaussian at the target's mean with half its spread.\n",
    "`MU`, `SD`, `tmin` and `tmax` are there to help you place components."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 104,
   "id": "cs09",
   "metadata": {},
